    "summary": "Use-after-free of a dictionary after a one-shot call on a context with an open stream",
    "details": "The one-shot `DCtx` and `CCtx` methods assumed the C library resets the\ncontext, but it leaves an open stream as it is. When a stream was left\nunfinished on a context, a one-shot call such as `decompress_using_dict`\ncould leave the context pointing at the dictionary borrowed for that call,\nand the next streaming call resumed the stream against it after it was\nfreed: decompressed output then contained freed heap memory. On the\ncompression side, the stream resumed against the one-shot call's buffers.\n\nThis requires an application to use one context for both streaming and\none-shot calls without a reset in between. The flaw was corrected by\nresetting the session after one-shot calls whenever a stream may be open.",
    "severity": [],
    "affected": [
      {
        "package": {
          "ecosystem": "crates.io",
          "name": "zstd-safe",
          "purl": "pkg:cargo/zstd-safe"
