    "summary": "`Seekable::decompress` sets a `Vec` length beyond its capacity for offsets past the end",
    "details": "`ZSTD_seekable_decompress` shortens the requested length to the end of the\ndata without checking that the offset is before it. For an offset past the\nend, it returns a wrapped-around length without writing anything, and\n`Seekable::decompress` passed that length to `Vec::set_len`.\n\nWith the `seekable` feature, whoever supplies the archive, or chooses the\noffset, can leave the caller's `Vec<u8>` with a length far beyond its\ncapacity. Reading it then discloses neighbouring heap memory, and appending\nto it corrupts memory. Offsets near `u64::MAX` can also hang the call.\n\nThe flaw was corrected by clamping requests to the end of the data, and by\nchecking every count reported by the C library against the buffer capacity.",
    "severity": [],
    "affected": [
      {
        "package": {
          "ecosystem": "crates.io",
          "name": "zstd-safe",
          "purl": "pkg:cargo/zstd-safe"
        },
