    "summary": "Heap buffer overflow in `CCtx::try_clone` on a multithreaded context",
    "details": "`CCtx::try_clone` (`experimental` feature, deprecated) copies tables sized\nfrom the context's applied parameters. Starting a multithreaded frame\n(`zstdmt` feature) replaces those parameters with the workers' without\nresizing the context's own tables, so after an abandoned single-threaded\nframe, the copy wrote up to 512 KiB past a heap allocation, or read past\none. This became reachable with the bundled zstd 1.5.6.\n\nThe flaw was corrected by refusing `try_clone` (and the unsafe\n`compress_block`) once `NbWorkers` was set on the context.",
