    "summary": "Use-after-free when changing a multithreaded context with an unfinished frame",
    "details": "When a multithreaded frame (`zstdmt` feature, `CParameter::NbWorkers`) is\nleft unfinished, its jobs may still be running on the worker threads: the C\nlibrary only waits for them when the next frame starts, or when the context\nis freed. A session reset makes the context accept changes again in the\nmeantime, so:\n\n- unloading the dictionary (`load_dictionary`, `ref_cdict`, `ref_prefix`,\n  `disable_dictionary`, `init*`, or `reset` with parameters) freed the\n  dictionary a worker was still compressing against;\n- changing `NbWorkers` made the next frame resize the job table before\n  waiting for the old jobs.\n\nThe flaw was corrected by refusing these calls while a multithreaded frame\nis unfinished. The new `CCtx::wait_for_workers()` waits for the workers\nfirst.",
    "severity": [],
